{"type": "assistant_complete", "text": "# Month-End Sales Reconciliation Report\n\n## Summary\n- **Full Matches:** 3\n- **Exceptions:** 4\n- **Total Impact Amount (CNY):** 1,250.00\n\n## Detail Table\n| Transaction ID | Discrepancy Type | CRM Amount (CNY) | Bank Amount (CNY) | Invoice Amount (CNY) | Variance (CNY) | Probable Cause |\n|----------------|------------------|------------------|-------------------|----------------------|----------------|----------------|\n| TX-1002        | Amount Discrepancy | 980.00           | 980.00            | 890.00               | 90.00          | Invoice amount does not match CRM and bank amounts. |\n| TX-1004        | Missing Invoice   | 730.00           | 730.00            | -                    | 730.00         | No corresponding invoice found for the transaction. |\n| TX-1005        | Amount Discrepancy | 2200.00          | 2150.00           | 2200.00              | 50.00          | Bank amount is less than the CRM and invoice amounts, likely due to a merchant reserve. |\n| UNMAPPED-7781  | Bank-only (Unmatched) | -               | 560.00            | -                    | 560.00         | The bank entry has no corresponding CRM or invoice record, possibly a manual transfer. |\n\n## Recommended Actions\n1. Investigate the discrepancy in the amount for `TX-1002` between the CRM and the invoice. Contact the client, Blue Harbor Supply, to confirm the correct amount and adjust the records as necessary.\n2. For `TX-1004`, identify why there is no corresponding invoice and create an invoice if it was missed, or document the reason if this is a legitimate exception.\n3. Review the merchant reserve policy with Silver Kite Foods (`TX-1005`) and ensure that the difference of 50.00 CNY is accounted for in the next settlement or through a separate adjustment.\n4. Verify the nature of the `UNMAPPED-7781` bank entry. If it is a valid transaction, update the CRM and generate the appropriate invoice. If it is an error, reverse the transaction.\n\nPlease review the above findings and take the recommended actions to resolve the exceptions."}
